(a) All persons desiring to obtain a occupation tax certificate to operate a bonding or professional surety company in the City shall file an application with the City Clerk on forms approved by the chief of police. The applicant must be an owner, partner, limited liability company member or majority stockholder in the enterprise.
(b) Each applicant shall submit the following information at a minimum:
(1) Trade name and business address;
(2) Applicant's name and residence address;
(3) Name and residence address of all interested persons, to include owners, partners, stockholders, limited liability company members, officers and directors together with financial and background information on these individuals;
(4) Manager's name and residence address;
(5) Employee's names, ages, and residence addresses, including all representatives who will function within the City on behalf of applicant; and
(6) Such other information as may be required by the City Clerk or chief of police.
(c) All applicants for a license to operate a bonding or professional surety company within the City and all employees of the business must be fingerprinted so as to conduct a background investigation of the applicant and shall furnish such further information as may be required by the City Clerk or the City Police Department, including the completion of an application and all accompanying documents.
(d) A fee in an amount approved by the Mayor and City Council shall be submitted with each application as the cost of conducting the investigation of applicant. The application forms and the current approved fee shall be kept on file in the office of the City Clerk.
(e) The license fee for the conduct of a bonding business shall be determined in accordance with section 6-602. The license shall be posted in a conspicuous place at the office of the bonding company, visible to any individual lawfully on the premises.
(Ord No. 00-09, 10-2-00; Ord. No. 04-17, § 1(A), 7-6-04)

